From 19ffa8aa3218f57f8bc52ce6b49db66dbcbebf4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jo-Philipp Wich <jo@mein.io>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 11:02:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] vm: release resource type prototypes before the final GC

Since "include: register resource type prototypes with VM" (343ebc2),
type prototypes are part of the VM value pool and are released by
ucv_freeall() during VM teardown. Releasing them again afterwards
results in a heap-use-after-free / double free:

==ERROR: AddressSanitizer: heap-use-after-free ...
    #0 ucv_put_value types.c
    #1 uc_vm_free vm.c
freed by thread T0 here:
    #1 ucv_gc_common types.c
    #2 uc_vm_free vm.c

Drop 5a79aa56c15ec45dbd3eaff73d7a500ff3873936, which predates the value
pool registration and relies on type prototypes living outside of the
GC value list.

[Bogdan Mircea: adapt unchanged hunk context for the source revision before
source-table teardown; inserted and removed code remains the upstream change.]

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/ucode-lang/ucode/commit/19ffa8aa3218f57f8bc52ce6b49db66dbcbebf4e]

Signed-off-by: Jo-Philipp Wich <jo@mein.io>
Signed-off-by: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>

---
 vm.c | 14 +++++++-------
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

--- a/vm.c
+++ b/vm.c
@@ -274,6 +274,12 @@ void uc_vm_free(uc_vm_t *vm)
 		vm->open_upvals = ref;
 	}
 
+	/* Resource type prototypes are part of the VM value pool, so release the
+	 * restype refs before the final GC; any references still held by
+	 * GC-managed values are dropped by ucv_freeall() itself. */
+	for (i = 0; i < vm->restypes.count; i++)
+		ucv_put(vm->restypes.entries[i]->proto);
+
 	uc_vm_reset_callframes(vm);
 	uc_vm_reset_stack(vm);
 	uc_vector_clear(&vm->stack);
@@ -283,14 +289,8 @@ void uc_vm_free(uc_vm_t *vm)
 
 	ucv_freeall(vm);
 
-	/* Type prototypes are not on the GC value list, so a ucv_put() during
-	 * ucv_freeall()'s retain phase would only mark them UC_NULL and leak
-	 * them. Release them here, after the final GC, so the last reference a
-	 * GC value may hold (e.g. via proto()) is already gone. */
-	for (i = 0; i < vm->restypes.count; i++) {
-		ucv_put(vm->restypes.entries[i]->proto);
+	for (i = 0; i < vm->restypes.count; i++)
 		free(vm->restypes.entries[i]);
-	}
 
 	uc_vector_clear(&vm->restypes);
 
